  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe current construction achieves C\u22480.38085. To find a lower bound, I use layered refinement:\n1. Starts with 400-point grid from `initial_h_values`\n2. Uses simulated annealing to explore finer-grained representations\n3. Employs two-phase optimization: global exploration followed by local refinement\n4. Applies constraint projection via `project_feasible` after each move\n\nKey innovations:\n1. Uses a cooling schedule with smarter temperature decay\n2. Incorporates probabilistic acceptance of worse moves\n3. Maintains parallel CD swaps and gradient projection\n4. Transfers solutions between grid sizes with projection\n5. Uses interpolated solutions as seeds for higher-resolution search\n\nMathematical specification:\nVariables: step function h: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1] with \u222bh dx=1\nObjective: minimize C = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\nConstraints: 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 \u2200i, \u2211h[i]\u00b7dx=1\n\nFor algorithm:\n1. Parameters:\n- Initial temperature: 0.9*distance_to_target\n- Annealing rate: 0.995\n- Swap probability: 0.8\n- Accept worse moves: exp(-\u0394C/temp)\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Parent solution handling:\n- Start by cloning and validating parent grid\n- Project to finer grid (doubling points) with integral enforcement\n\n2. Core optimization:\n- Maintain candidate and best solutions\n- Time tracking: evaluate every N steps\n- CD swaps: periodic changes to h[i]-h[j] using change matrix\n- Stochastic swaps: random resampling with acceptance\n- Gradient projection: coordinate-wise subgradient descent\n\n3. Temperature management:\n- Initiate cooling based on stationarity time\n- Decay: T_new = max(0.001, T*0.995)\n- Stop when temperature too small OR time expired\n\n4. Intervals:\n- Cooldown periods: \u22655% improvement to trigger annealing\n- Pause at grid doublings: 800, 1600 points\n- Progressive resolution: from 400\u2192800\u21921600\u21923200 points\n\n5. Solver:\n- Sample from initial guess (CD swaps)\n- Apply gradient projection after every N accepted swaps\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Swap sizes: two-point swaps follows by block swaps\n- Checkpoint: save every 1000 steps\n- Restart strategy: halve the system when plateauing\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- Double grid every 200 seconds, max 3\u00d7resolution\n- Project feasibility after every move\n- Handle dimension changes via interpolation\n- Continuous monitoring: abort excessive time usage\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Check \u2211h[i]\u00b7dx=0.5\u00b7n exactly\n- Ensure all h[i]\u2208[0,1]\n- Compute final score via exact correlation\n- Return solution if time allows\n- Output best solution found, no penalty for unmet constraints\n\nValidation steps:\n1. Verify dx=2/n parameter\n2. Check feasibility before calling compute_c5\n3. Ensure objective evaluation uses mode='full'\n4. Reject solutions that violate constraints\n5. Maintain detailed timing estimates",
